<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>High vs Low Resistance Liquidity Run - ICT Study</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;700&family=Crimson+Pro:wght@400;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-primary: #0a0a0f;
            --bg-card: #1a1a24;
            --bg-card-hover: #242433;
            --text-primary: #e8e8ed;
            --text-secondary: #9898a8;
            --accent-bear: #ff4757;
            --accent-bull: #2ed573;
            --accent-gold: #ffa502;
            --border-color: #2a2a3a;
        }

        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Crimson Pro', serif;
            background: var(--bg-primary);
            color: var(--text-primary);
            line-height: 1.7;
            font-size: 18px;
        }

        header {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a24 0%, #0f0f14 100%);
            padding: 4rem 2rem 3rem;
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-gold);
            text-align: center;
        }

        header h1 {
            font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--accent-gold);
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            letter-spacing: -0.5px;
        }

        header p {
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        .timestamp {
            font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--accent-bull);
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }

        nav {
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
            background: rgba(26, 26, 36, 0.95);
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            padding: 1rem 2rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            display: flex;
            gap: 1.5rem;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: center;
            z-index: 100;
        }

        nav a {
            font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
            font-size: 0.875rem;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            text-decoration: none;
            padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
            border-radius: 6px;
            transition: all 0.2s;
        }

        nav a:hover {
            background: var(--bg-card-hover);
            color: var(--accent-gold);
        }

        main {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 3rem 2rem 6rem;
        }

        section {
            margin-bottom: 5rem;
            scroll-margin-top: 100px;
        }

        section h2 {
            font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
            font-size: 2rem;
            color: var(--accent-gold);
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
            padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border-color);
        }

        section h3 {
            font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            color: var(--text-primary);
            margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
        }

        .quote {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-gold);
            padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
            font-style: italic;
        }

        .quote em {
            color: var(--accent-gold);
            font-style: normal;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .concept-card {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
        }

        .concept-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-2px);
            box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.1);
        }

        .card-header {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: space-between;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }

        .card-title {
            font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
            font-size: 1rem;
            color: var(--accent-gold);
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .flashcard-container {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
            gap: 1.5rem;
            margin-top: 2rem;
        }

        .flashcard {
            background: var(--bg-card);
            border: 2px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 2rem;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.3s;
            min-height: 200px;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            position: relative;
        }

        .flashcard:hover {
            border-color: var(--accent-gold);
            transform: scale(1.02);
        }

        .flashcard-question {
            font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            color: var(--text-primary);
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .flashcard-answer {
            font-style: italic;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            margin-top: 1rem;
            display: none;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            padding-top: 1rem;
        }

        .flashcard.revealed .flashcard-answer {
            display: block;
        }

        .flashcard.revealed .flashcard-question::after {
            content: " ✓";
            color: var(--accent-bull);
        }

        svg {
            max-width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            margin: 2rem 0;
            background: var(--bg-card);
            padding: 2rem;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        ul, ol {
            margin: 1rem 0 1rem 2rem;
        }

        li {
            margin: 0.5rem 0;
            color: var(--text-primary);
        }

        strong {
            color: var(--accent-gold);
        }

        code {
            font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
            background: var(--bg-card);
            padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-size: 0.9em;
            color: var(--accent-bull);
        }

        .warning-box {
            background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.1);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-bear);
            padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
        }

        .success-box {
            background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.1);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-bull);
            padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
        }

        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            header h1 {
                font-size: 2rem;
            }

            section h2 {
                font-size: 1.5rem;
            }

            .flashcard-container {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>How to Know if a Swing Point is Highly Defended</h1>
        <p>High Resistance vs Low Resistance Liquidity Runs</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <a href="#definition">Definition</a>
        <a href="#liquidity">Liquidity Fundamentals</a>
        <a href="#high-resistance">High Resistance</a>
        <a href="#low-resistance">Low Resistance</a>
        <a href="#institutional">Institutional View</a>
        <a href="#study">Study</a>
    </nav>

    <main>
        <section id="definition">
            <h2>Core Definition</h2>
            <div class="timestamp">[0:00-2:54]</div>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"liquidity as it relates to ICT Concepts it relates to buy orders and sell orders it's as simple as that"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Buy Liquidity (Above Old Highs)</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"their stop loss order would be resting right above this high or generally many times just rate at that high"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"there's going to be above old highs and Below old lows"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"buy stop or buy liquidity above that high"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Sell Liquidity (Below Old Lows)</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"sell liquidity"</em> below old lows</p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="liquidity">
            <h2>Liquidity Fundamentals</h2>
            <div class="timestamp">[0:00-2:54]</div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Where Liquidity Resides</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"there's going to be above old highs and Below old lows"</em></p>
            </div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Stop Loss Placement</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"their stop loss order would be resting right above this high or generally many times just rate at that high"</em></p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="high-resistance">
            <h2>High Resistance Liquidity Run</h2>
            <div class="timestamp">[3:06-6:39]</div>

            <h3>Definition</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"when we see the market give this thick area of resistance okay there's a lot of price action that the market has to trade through to get back to an old high of significance we view this as a high resistance liquidity run"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Visual Structure</h3>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 800 500" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <!-- Title -->
                <text x="400" y="30" fill="#ffa502" font-size="20" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">High Resistance Liquidity Run</text>

                <!-- Old High (Target) -->
                <line x1="50" y1="100" x2="750" y2="100" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5,5"/>
                <text x="760" y="105" fill="#2ed573" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Old High</text>
                <text x="400" y="90" fill="#2ed573" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">(Buy Liquidity Above)</text>

                <!-- Thick Area of Resistance - Multiple Highs and Lows -->
                <rect x="100" y="120" width="600" height="200" fill="none" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
                <text x="400" y="145" fill="#ff4757" font-size="16" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Thick Area of Resistance</text>
                <text x="400" y="165" fill="#ff4757" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">"a lot of price action that the market has to trade through"</text>

                <!-- Multiple Previous Highs -->
                <line x1="150" y1="180" x2="250" y2="180" stroke="#e8e8ed" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="250" cy="180" r="4" fill="#ff4757"/>
                <text x="255" y="175" fill="#9898a8" font-size="11">Previous High</text>

                <line x1="300" y1="200" x2="400" y2="200" stroke="#e8e8ed" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="400" cy="200" r="4" fill="#ff4757"/>
                <text x="405" y="195" fill="#9898a8" font-size="11">Previous High</text>

                <line x1="450" y1="220" x2="550" y2="220" stroke="#e8e8ed" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="550" cy="220" r="4" fill="#ff4757"/>
                <text x="555" y="215" fill="#9898a8" font-size="11">Previous High</text>

                <!-- Multiple Previous Lows -->
                <line x1="200" y1="260" x2="300" y2="260" stroke="#e8e8ed" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="200" cy="260" r="4" fill="#2ed573"/>
                <text x="205" y="275" fill="#9898a8" font-size="11">Previous Low</text>

                <line x1="350" y1="240" x2="450" y2="240" stroke="#e8e8ed" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="350" cy="240" r="4" fill="#2ed573"/>
                <text x="355" y="255" fill="#9898a8" font-size="11">Previous Low</text>

                <line x1="500" y1="280" x2="600" y2="280" stroke="#e8e8ed" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <circle cx="500" cy="280" r="4" fill="#2ed573"/>
                <text x="505" y="295" fill="#9898a8" font-size="11">Previous Low</text>

                <!-- Arrows showing resistance -->
                <path d="M 400 310 L 400 110" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead-resist)"/>
                <text x="410" y="210" fill="#ff4757" font-size="13" font-weight="bold">Hard to penetrate</text>

                <!-- Current Price Area -->
                <line x1="50" y1="350" x2="750" y2="350" stroke="#ffa502" stroke-width="3"/>
                <text x="760" y="355" fill="#ffa502" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Current Price</text>

                <!-- Annotations -->
                <text x="400" y="390" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle">"the Market's going to have a very hard time getting through</text>
                <text x="400" y="410" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle">all of these previous lows and previous highs"</text>

                <text x="400" y="450" fill="#ff4757" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Least Probable Trading Condition for Longs</text>
                <text x="400" y="470" fill="#9898a8" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">"so many levels of resistance"</text>

                <!-- Arrow marker definition -->
                <defs>
                    <marker id="arrowhead-resist" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto">
                        <polygon points="0 0, 10 3, 0 6" fill="#ff4757" />
                    </marker>
                </defs>
            </svg>

            <h3>Market Difficulty</h3>
            <div class="warning-box">
                <p><em>"the Market's going to have a very hard time getting through all of these previous lows and previous highs"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h3>Trading Implication</h3>
            <div class="warning-box">
                <p><em>"this is the least probable trading condition to look for Longs because you have so many levels of resistance"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h3>Highly Defended Stops</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"those individuals with stops above this old high in the form of a fund they're actually very highly defended because of this type of price action"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>What It Takes to Break Through</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"it's going to take a very uh sharp economic Market release the data kind of like nonfarm payroll or fomc that type of event will knock through all these levels of resistance"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Universal Application</h3>
            <div class="timestamp">[4:14-4:18]</div>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"this is not specific to any time frame it's Universal"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="low-resistance">
            <h2>Low Resistance Liquidity Run</h2>
            <div class="timestamp">[6:56-11:21]</div>

            <h3>Definition</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"a low resistance liquidity run would be in the form of something similar to this if we see the market come off a old high and it comes down rather quickly if there is a very sharp or one-way type Direction very little uh retracements of any kind"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Visual Structure</h3>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 800 500" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <!-- Title -->
                <text x="400" y="30" fill="#ffa502" font-size="20" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Low Resistance Liquidity Run</text>

                <!-- Old High (Starting Point) -->
                <line x1="50" y1="100" x2="750" y2="100" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5,5"/>
                <text x="760" y="105" fill="#ff4757" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Old High</text>

                <!-- Sharp One-Way Move Down - Very Little Price Action -->
                <path d="M 150 100 L 180 150 L 170 160 L 200 200 L 190 210 L 220 260 L 210 270 L 240 350"
                      stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="4" fill="none"/>

                <text x="100" y="230" fill="#2ed573" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" transform="rotate(-70 100 230)">Sharp Move</text>
                <text x="260" y="180" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="12">"comes down rather quickly"</text>
                <text x="260" y="200" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="12">"very sharp or one-way type Direction"</text>
                <text x="260" y="220" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="12">"very little retracements of any kind"</text>

                <!-- Minimal Retracements (shown as small pullbacks) -->
                <circle cx="180" cy="150" r="5" fill="#ffa502" opacity="0.6"/>
                <text x="190" y="150" fill="#9898a8" font-size="11">Minimal retracement</text>

                <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="5" fill="#ffa502" opacity="0.6"/>
                <circle cx="220" cy="260" r="5" fill="#ffa502" opacity="0.6"/>

                <!-- Clean Area (Very Little Price Action) -->
                <rect x="120" y="110" width="160" height="260" fill="none" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
                <text x="300" y="250" fill="#2ed573" font-size="13" font-weight="bold">Very Little Resistance</text>

                <!-- Current Price / Target Area -->
                <line x1="50" y1="350" x2="750" y2="350" stroke="#ffa502" stroke-width="3"/>
                <text x="760" y="355" fill="#ffa502" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Old Low (Target)</text>
                <text x="400" y="340" fill="#2ed573" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">(Sell Liquidity Below)</text>

                <!-- Easy Path Arrow -->
                <path d="M 500 120 L 500 330" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead-easy)"/>
                <text x="510" y="220" fill="#2ed573" font-size="13" font-weight="bold">Easy Path</text>
                <text x="510" y="240" fill="#2ed573" font-size="12">"hot knife through butter"</text>

                <!-- Retracement Illustration -->
                <text x="400" y="390" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle">"this is the easiest area to trade in price action because</text>
                <text x="400" y="410" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle">you have very little resistance allowing price to just cut through all that"</text>

                <text x="400" y="450" fill="#2ed573" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Easiest Time to Trade in the Marketplace</text>
                <text x="400" y="470" fill="#2ed573" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">"every retracement is going to find very little resistance"</text>

                <!-- Arrow marker definition -->
                <defs>
                    <marker id="arrowhead-easy" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto">
                        <polygon points="0 0, 10 3, 0 6" fill="#2ed573" />
                    </marker>
                </defs>
            </svg>

            <h3>Trading Advantage</h3>
            <div class="success-box">
                <p><em>"this is the easiest area to trade in price action because you have very little resistance allowing price to just cut through all that"</em></p>
            </div>

            <div class="success-box">
                <p><em>"this is the easiest time to trade in the marketplace"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h3>Retracement Behavior</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"every retracement is going to find very little resistance"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Hot Knife Through Butter</h3>
            <div class="timestamp">[13:21-13:26]</div>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"it's like a hot knife through butter very little resistance to every time a low is formed price goes through those lows"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="institutional">
            <h2>Institutional Perspective</h2>
            <div class="timestamp">[17:03-17:32]</div>

            <h3>Defended Levels</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"the more price action there is around a specific level or a high or a low that is indicating a levels being defended on an Institutional price Model"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Synchronization with Institutional Order Flow</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you're going to be getting yourself in sync with the institutional order flow then your trades will find very low resistance in the form of profitable exits and very little draw down"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="study">
            <h2>Study & Review</h2>
            <p>Click each card to reveal the answer (from transcript quotes)</p>

            <div class="flashcard-container">
                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What is liquidity as it relates to ICT Concepts?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"liquidity as it relates to ICT Concepts it relates to buy orders and sell orders it's as simple as that"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Where is buy liquidity located in relation to old highs?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"buy stop or buy liquidity above that high" - "their stop loss order would be resting right above this high or generally many times just rate at that high"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What defines a High Resistance Liquidity Run?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"when we see the market give this thick area of resistance okay there's a lot of price action that the market has to trade through to get back to an old high of significance we view this as a high resistance liquidity run"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Why is High Resistance Liquidity Run the least probable trading condition for longs?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"this is the least probable trading condition to look for Longs because you have so many levels of resistance"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What makes stops highly defended in a High Resistance scenario?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"those individuals with stops above this old high in the form of a fund they're actually very highly defended because of this type of price action"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What type of event is needed to break through high resistance?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"it's going to take a very uh sharp economic Market release the data kind of like nonfarm payroll or fomc that type of event will knock through all these levels of resistance"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What defines a Low Resistance Liquidity Run?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"a low resistance liquidity run would be in the form of something similar to this if we see the market come off a old high and it comes down rather quickly if there is a very sharp or one-way type Direction very little uh retracements of any kind"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Why is Low Resistance the easiest area to trade?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"this is the easiest area to trade in price action because you have very little resistance allowing price to just cut through all that"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">How do retracements behave in Low Resistance conditions?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"every retracement is going to find very little resistance"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What does the "hot knife through butter" metaphor describe?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"it's like a hot knife through butter very little resistance to every time a low is formed price goes through those lows"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Are High and Low Resistance concepts time frame specific?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"this is not specific to any time frame it's Universal"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What does more price action around a level indicate from an institutional perspective?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"the more price action there is around a specific level or a high or a low that is indicating a levels being defended on an Institutional price Model"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What happens when you sync with institutional order flow?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"you're going to be getting yourself in sync with the institutional order flow then your trades will find very low resistance in the form of profitable exits and very little draw down"</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <script>
        // Smooth scrolling for navigation
        document.querySelectorAll('nav a').forEach(anchor => {
            anchor.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                const target = document.querySelector(this.getAttribute('href'));
                target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
            });
        });

        // Keyboard navigation for flashcards
        document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e) {
            if (e.key === 'Enter' && e.target.closest('.flashcard')) {
                e.target.closest('.flashcard').classList.toggle('revealed');
            }
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>